--- !u!114 &2895851072768369960
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'Indirect lighting calculations in real-time are incredibly costly on most hardware platforms. Therefore, <b>baking</b> or precomputing the indirect lighting is an important step.


      Baked lighting in Unity rely on lightmaps, which are textures that store the lighting information that can be used at runtime to greatly speed up the rendering of the (indirect) lighting.


      The image above shows the exact same Scene after the baked lighting data has been removed. As you can see, the bounce lighting is missing and the indirect lighting relies only on the ambient lighting generated from the Sky, making the interior look abnormally bright and flat.'
